  "restoration_note": "Teaching gives a correspondential taxonomy of natural begetting (the enthumesis of death printed at three depths — root, branch, seed; abortions, mutual generation, self-molding) followed by the parthenos/enkratēs doctrine at four ascending registers (celestial Light untouched / mingled-and-returned / Mind of Light bearing the elect / regenerate man stripped of Sin). Restorations are most secure in the parthenos/enkratēs section (chs. 98), where the formulaic repetition of 'whom they call X is Y' and the recurring keywords ⲡⲁⲣⲑⲉⲛⲟⲥ, ⲉⲅⲕⲣⲁⲧⲏⲥ, ⲉⲛⲑⲩⲙⲏⲥⲓⲥ, ⲕⲁⲣⲡⲟⲥ, ⲥⲁⲣⲝ, ⲡⲣⲉⲥⲃⲉⲩⲧⲏⲥ, and the parallel 'has not tasted death, neither has come to the war' anchor word-completions. Several editor proposals were overridden where position-numbering in the apparatus pointed to a different anchor letter (notably {141}=ⲛ for ⲧⲍⲓⲕⲱⲛ, {143}=ⲕ for ⲁϩⲃⲱⲕ, {150}=ⲣⲱ for ⲣⲱⲙⲉ). The botanical-typological middle of ch.97 (lines 6-24) is too damaged across multiple consecutive medium lacunae to warrant invented fills; those are honestly left unrestorable. The closing dragon/teaching coda (ch.100.23) is also too fragmentary.",
